<title>GERMANY: Holzmann -no cap rise before better profit.</title>
<headline>Holzmann -no cap rise before better profit.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>German construction group Philipp Holzmann AG Chief Financial Officer Rainer Klee said on Wednesday that the company would only be in a position to increase its capital when its earnings improved.</p>
<p>&quot;A capital raising can only be realised when Holzmann returns to generating good results,&quot; Klee told the annual shareholders' meeting.</p>
<p>Earlier, Holzmann said it would post another operating loss in 1997 after a loss of 300 million marks in 1996.</p>
<p>-- David Crossland, Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525</p>
</text>
